===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ru|orv|кубъ||[[drinking]] [[vessel]]}}, {{etydate|14th century|nocap=1}}, further origin uncertain.

Cognate with {{cog|uk|куб||[[wooden]] [[dish]]}}, {{cog|pl|kubek||[[bowl]], [[cup]]}}, {{cog|dsb|kub||[[bowl]], [[cup]]}}, also {{m|dsb|kubk}}.

Per Vasmer, likely related to {{noncog|sa|कुम्भ|t=[[pot]]}}, {{noncog|ae|𐬑𐬎𐬨𐬠𐬀|t=[[pot]]}}, {{noncog|grc|κύμβος||[[vessel]]}}, {{m|grc|κύβη||[[cup]]}}, also {{m|grc|κύμβη}}.

However Trubachev notes that there are no signs of a nasal vowel and reconstructs {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*kubъ}}, thus rejecting a possible link to {{noncog|ine-pro|*kumbʰo-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kumbʰéh₂-||vessel}} and proposing a connection to {{m|ine-pro||*koubʰ-}}.

